    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/0/90146.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 20,
    "turn_text": "You know what's interesting about today's episode is that we've reached out to Speaker Pelosi's office multiple times today. I only asked you earlier today to be on it five minutes later. We requested to the speaker's office to be here and actually debate this. She was told she was not able to make it. But you are one of the few people in this country that actually gets face to face time with the Speaker of the House and actually is in these negotiations. And so there's a public narrative of why the Democrats claim that they're on the moral high ground for delaying this. And they claim that They made it better that they added all this funding that we refused to add. What's the truth behind this? Let's go over her arguments. How did this play out when the Treasury said, hey, we need another quarter trillion dollars, $250 billion, and in the Senate, Mitch McConnell said, we're ready to do this. Of course, Republicans in the House are ready to do this. What was their objection?",
