    "turn_idx": 31,
    "turn_text": "And it wasn't just Schumer, his own members were in there writing this bill. Pelosi comes into the room and Schumer changes a different person. And what's most interesting about this is they start arguing over one or two lines. And just a week prior, we had a bill come to the floor that came out of the house. It was the second supplemental bill we did. At midnight that night, the language still was not correct. But what I said to Nancy Pelosi, I'm okay with taking it to the floor on this agreement. It's not the way we have talked about it, but we'll correct this on Monday because I don't want the American public saying, We've got problems. We're going to fight this together. We're going to be bipartisan. And on the Republican, when this came, because they couldn't get the language and time done, the people writing it, we did a handshake and we voted for it overwhelmingly. And then we corrected on Monday. She holds it up and then she starts making this argument. She starts talking about the November election, Planned Parenthood, and the Green New Deal. I literally turned to her and I said, I'm not holding up the American public and our economy and our healthcare based upon you worried about what the November election is going to look like.",
