    "turn_text": "and now we're going to add another seventy five states have a hundred and fifty for the states and cities we have in the last month given them five hundred billion dollars now let's put this in perspective because i love what you do then you you stick to just facts We spend approximately a little over $600 billion a year in Medicare, and we in one month have given the states $500 billion. So when you talk about accountability in others, we don't know how much states will need more, but there's 150 billion sitting there that is going to go out later this month. So on April 7, the only account that was going to run out of money based upon the speed in which it was going was small business. The only thing the small business did was 75% of this money, if you took it, had to pay employees whether you're working or not. And this is the philosophy behind the bill. We're not in this problem because we have a financial crisis like before, because China lied. We have a virus. Government tells businesses to shut down. We do not want these people to have to go to unemployment. So the first thing we do is we send checks to individuals so they could pay their rent, pay their mortgage based upon how much they make, 75,000. Then if you have a small business, we told you shut, we're going to provide you not alone, but a grant. And for it to be a grant, you have to give it to your employees and we're paying it through there. So we were thinking two months, we give you two and a half, get through this and we open back up. Then the third part and a small business is that any person that has 500 employees or fewer. And really when you look at it, the 74% of the loans were less than $60,000 in payroll a month. So they really are small businesses. Then for the larger businesses, we helped them get a loan and we did a tax credit for retention tax credit where we'd pay up to almost 50% of your employees for those two months. The whole idea was you didn't want to create a financial crisis where people weren't getting money or paid. So now they're not paying for their house, they're not paying for their rent.",
